<title>CANADA: Maple Leaf Foods raises local hog premium.</title>
<headline>Maple Leaf Foods raises local hog premium.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maple Leaf Foods Inc, Canada's largest food processor, said it would increase the local premium paid for Alberta hogs by C$2 per animal to $9.</p>
<p>&quot;We plan to process hogs long-term in the region and we intend to continue buying our fair share of hogs. We will work with the Alberta Pork Producers Development Corporation and directly with producers to ensure this goal is achieved,&quot; Maple Leaf Foods president and chairman Michael McCain said.</p>
<p>Maple Leaf Foods operates the Gainers pork facility in Edmonton, Alberta.</p>
<p>(Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720)</p>
